    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d462">

                <pb facs="1015" n="983" xml:id="pg983"/>

                <head>462. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Thailand<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d462-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-01-24T20:26:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                                1958—8:26 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1931. Joint State–ICA–Defense. Department’s 1102.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d462-f2"/>
                    Despite inclusion in Thai Cabinet several ministers whose foreign policy views
                    are questionable, appears from official position taken by Government leaders
                    (example Government policy statement and Thanom New Year address), as well as
                    Embassy analysis (Embtel 1896)<anchor n="3" xml:id="d462-f3"/> that Government
                    is maintaining favorable posture re collective security, Communism and Free
                    World. Therefore unless you see objection we are prepared proceed with normal
                    programming and obligational process for current fiscal year.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d462-f4"/></p>
                <p>For USOM: Have received and are processing FY 58 operational program (Toica
                        A–989).<anchor n="5" xml:id="d462-f5"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d462-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d462-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 792.00/1–2458. Secret. Drafted by
                    Bushner and Walter G. Stoneman of ICA, cleared with the Department of Defense,
                    and approved by Gardner Palmer.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d462-f2" n="2" xml:id="d462-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 1102, October 24, 1957, State, ICA, and Defense expressed concurrence
                    in the aid program approach proposed in telegram 1056 from Bangkok October 5,
                    1957, which is printed in <ref target="frus1955-57v22#pg_938"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1955–1957, vol. XXII, p.
                        938</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d462-f3" n="3" xml:id="d462-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d458-f3">footnote 3, Document 458</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d462-f4" n="4" xml:id="d462-f4-content">
                <p>In telegram 2190 from Bangkok, January 28, the Country Team concurred.
                    (Department of State, Central Files, 792.00/1–2858)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d462-f5" n="5" xml:id="d462-f5-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
